  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Back-and-forth games expose who you are. This one exposed the Giants' inability to finish what they started.",
    "what_this_means": "They led after three innings. San Diego tied it in the fourth. The Giants scratched back in the eighth. Basabe doubled them level. But never got the go-ahead run home. Mahle threw 5.2 solid innings. The bullpen held clean. Twelve hits, two runs on runners in scoring position, and they lost by one. This is what inconsistency looks like when it's not random: they get to the moment and can't execute. The pitching gave them air. The bats wasted it.",
    "what_to_watch": "Michael King has a 3.38 ERA and San Diego's offense has been quiet lately. Roupp's last four starts saw him post a 2.60 ERA. Tonight, the Giants need one of these to break. Either their timing at the plate or King's recent form. First pitch at 1:10 PT.",
